cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use erpax, cite it by its content-addressed release DOI."
title: "erpax — a zero-entropy, content-addressed ERP corpus"
abstract: >-
  erpax is an ERP corpus in which every folder under src/ is one irreducible atom
  told three ways (form · code · proof), wired through a single content-uuid.
  Its law is zero entropy ⇒ infinite tamper-cost: a claim is enforced by a gate
  that blocks its violation, never by prose that asks for compliance.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rouschev
    given-names: Tsvetan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7312-9778"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22237698"
identifiers:
  # The CONCEPT doi resolves to the newest version, always — cite this one unless you mean a
  # specific release. The VERSION doi is the frozen record of exactly these bytes.
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22237698"
    description: "Concept DOI — every version of erpax"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22288360"
    description: "Version DOI — v1.0.3, corpus fold 600417d1-8eff-82ef-8d4f-7ade48e9ea3e"
repository-code: "https://github.com/erpax/erpax"
url: "https://github.com/erpax/erpax"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"
contact:
  - email: "license@erpax.com"
    name: "erpax licensing"
version: 1.0.3
keywords:
  - ERP
  - content-addressing
  - double-entry accounting
  - provenance
  - tamper-evidence
  - compliance-as-code

# PRIOR ART, BY DOMAIN — the published work erpax builds on, not a claim about what is novel
# in it. A DOI dates a disclosure; it does not adjudicate priority against anyone else's.
#
# EVERY entry here was verified rather than remembered: each DOI was resolved and its title
# read back from Crossref or the RFC Editor before it was written down. Ten candidates were
# checked and four discarded — they resolved perfectly and were about capital-market research,
# ransomware taxonomy, a conference proceedings volume and microservice migration. A resolving
# pointer to the wrong work is worse than no pointer, which is the rule this corpus enforces on
# its own citations (rules/reference) and had no business exempting itself from.
#
#   DOMAIN 1 · content addressing and tamper evidence — the same content is the same name,
#              and a change to a sealed record is detectable rather than forbidden
#   DOMAIN 2 · software quality and audit — a quality claim is a gate, and a citation must
#              lead to its evidence
#   DOMAIN 3 · fiscal and statutory — the clause→code trace an inspector walks
references:
  # ── DOMAIN 1 · content addressing and tamper evidence ──────────────────────────────────
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "A Digital Signature Based on a Conventional Encryption Function"
    authors:
      - family-names: Merkle
        given-names: "Ralph C."
    year: 1988
    collection-title: "Advances in Cryptology — CRYPTO '87, Lecture Notes in Computer Science"
    doi: "10.1007/3-540-48184-2_32"
    notes: >-
      The hash tree. erpax folds its corpus to one root the same way, which is what makes a
      whole-corpus seal checkable without reading the corpus.
  - type: article
    title: "How to time-stamp a digital document"
    authors:
      - family-names: Haber
        given-names: Stuart
      - family-names: Stornetta
        given-names: "W. Scott"
    year: 1991
    journal: "Journal of Cryptology"
    doi: "10.1007/BF00196791"
    notes: >-
      Dating a document without trusting the dater. The ancestor of every content-addressed
      provenance claim erpax makes, including the one this citation record is part of.
  - type: standard
    title: "RFC 6962 — Certificate Transparency"
    authors:
      - name: "Internet Engineering Task Force"
    year: 2013
    doi: "10.17487/RFC6962"
    url: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6962"
    notes: >-
      Append-only logs whose consistency anyone can verify — the shape of erpax's audit chain,
      where a receipt is checkable by a party who trusts nobody.
  - type: standard
    title: "RFC 9562 — Universally Unique IDentifiers (UUIDs)"
    authors:
      - name: "Internet Engineering Task Force"
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.17487/RFC9562"
    url: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562"
    notes: >-
      §5.8 defines the v8 custom UUID. erpax's content-uuid is a v8 folded from an atom's
      content, so the same content is the same address on any machine, in any order.
  - type: standard
    title: "RFC 8785 — JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)"
    authors:
      - name: "Internet Engineering Task Force"
    year: 2020
    doi: "10.17487/RFC8785"
    url: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8785"
    notes: >-
      The canonical serialization erpax folds before hashing. Without it key order would change
      an address, and content-addressing would not hold at all.

  # ── DOMAIN 2 · software quality and audit ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  - type: standard
    title: "ISO/IEC 25010:2023 — Systems and software Quality Requirements and Evaluation (SQuaRE): product quality model"
    authors:
      - name: "International Organization for Standardization"
    year: 2023
    url: "https://www.iso.org/standard/78176.html"
    notes: >-
      Each quality characteristic erpax cites is reverse-engineered into an executable gate; a
      characteristic cited with no gate behind it is itself a tracked violation.
  - type: standard
    title: "ISO 19011:2018 — Guidelines for auditing management systems"
    authors:
      - name: "International Organization for Standardization"
    year: 2018
    url: "https://www.iso.org/standard/70017.html"
    notes: >-
      §6.4 audit evidence — a citation must lead to its evidence. erpax gates every src/…
      pointer in its own prose on this, at zero tolerance on the statutory surface.

  # ── DOMAIN 3 · fiscal and statutory ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - type: standard
    title: "Наредба № Н-18 — Bulgarian fiscal-device and SUPTO regulation"
    authors:
      - name: "Ministry of Finance of the Republic of Bulgaria"
    year: 2006
    url: "https://lex.bg/laws/ldoc/2135540645"
    notes: >-
      The statutory surface erpax implements for Bulgarian fiscalisation — the УНП-carrying
      receipt, сторно reversal, the Приложение-38 audit file. Its clause→code trace is gated at
      zero dead pointers, because an unreviewable citation cannot be relied on.
